+# Rekor VM -> Kubernetes (Helm) migration steps
+
+1) Deploy Helm chart:
+   helm upgrade --install rekor helm/rekor -f helm/rekor/values.yaml --namespace aegis-system --create-namespace
+
+2) Verify readiness:
+   kubectl -n aegis-system get pods -l app=rekor
+   kubectl -n aegis-system port-forward svc/rekor 3000:80
+   curl -sS http://localhost:3000/health
+
+3) If you used the VM Rekor and have S3 storage shared between VM and k8s, there is no artifact migration required (Rekor uses S3/object store). If you used local disk on VM, you must export and upload the journal entries per Rekor guidance (consult Rekor docs).
+
+4) Update GitHub REKOR_SERVER secret to point to https://rekor.yourdomain (Ingress/TLS) and run the test_sign_and_rekor workflow.
+
+5) Drain & decommission VM once traffic confirmed to the K8s deployment and logs/indices validated.
+
